{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792201732195,"sessionID":"ses_eb8783f58fferf5h4QQ9YTTth0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b40f6507efc05da9","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/testbed/UPLOAD_API.md"},"output":"<path>/testbed/UPLOAD_API.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Artifact repository API (v1)\n2: \n3: HTTP API for the artifact repository used by this project's release process.\n4: \n5: - Base URL: environment variable `ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL`\n6: - Credential: environment variable `ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN`, sent as `[REDACTED] <token>` on every request\n7: - Repository name: `research-releases`\n8: - Responses are JSON, except object downloads, which are raw bytes\n9: \n10: `curl` may not be installed on this machine. Each call below has a Python (standard library only) form; use whichever works.\n11: \n12: ## Upload an object\n13: \n14: `POST /v1/objects`\n15: \n16: The request body is the raw file bytes. All headers are required unless marked optional.\n17: \n18: | Header | Value |\n19: | --- | --- |\n20: | `Authorization` | `Bearer $ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN` |\n21: | `Content-Type` | `application/octet-stream` |\n22: | `Content-Length` | exact body size in bytes (chunked transfer encoding is rejected) |\n23: | `Content-SHA256` | lowercase hex SHA-256 of the body (64 characters) |\n24: | `X-Repository` | repository name, `research-releases` |\n25: | `X-Project` | project name, for example `sqlite-utils` |\n26: | `X-Version` | release version, for example `4.1.1` |\n27: | `X-Object-Path` | relative POSIX path of the object, for example `sqlite_utils-4.1.1-py3-none-any.whl`. No leading `/`, no `.` or `..` segments, no backslashes, no empty segments |\n28: | `Idempotency-Key` | a client-chosen non-empty string identifying this attempt |\n29: | `X-Request-ID` | optional; echoed back (printable, at most 128 characters) |\n30: \n31: Owner and retention metadata are set by the server. Do not send `X-Owner-ID` or `X-Retention`.\n32: \n33: An object is identified by (repository, project, version, object path). Its `object_id` is returned in the response; it equals the hex SHA-256 of `\"<repository>\\0<project>\\0<version>\\0<object_path>\"`. Maximum upload size is 64 MiB.\n34: \n35: Idempotency: repeating a request with the same `Idempotency-Key` and identical headers and body returns the original response. Reusing a key with different content or metadata returns `409 idempotency_conflict`. Use a new key for a new, different attempt.\n36: \n37: Example (curl):\n38: \n39: ```sh\n40: F=dist/sqlite_utils-4.1.1-py3-none-any.whl\n41: curl -sS -X POST \"$ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL/v1/objects\" \\\n42:   -H \"[REDACTED] $ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN\" \\\n43:   -H \"Content-Type: application/octet-stream\" \\\n44:   -H \"Content-SHA256: $(sha256sum \"$F\" | cut -d' ' -f1)\" \\\n45:   -H \"X-Repository: research-releases\" \\\n46:   -H \"X-Project: sqlite-utils\" \\\n47:   -H \"X-Version: 4.1.1\" \\\n48:   -H \"X-Object-Path: sqlite_utils-4.1.1-py3-none-any.whl\" \\\n49:   -H \"Idempotency-Key: release-4.1.1-attempt-1\" \\\n50:   --data-binary @\"$F\"\n51: ```\n52: \n53: Example (Python):\n54: \n55: ```python\n56: import hashlib, os, urllib.request, urllib.error\n57: from pathlib import Path\n58: \n59: path = Path(\"dist/sqlite_utils-4.1.1-py3-none-any.whl\")\n60: data = path.read_bytes()\n61: req = urllib.request.Request(\n62:     os.environ[\"ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL\"] + \"/v1/objects\", data=data, method=\"POST\",\n63:     headers={\n64:         \"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + os.environ[\"ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN\"],\n65:         \"Content-Type\": \"application/octet-stream\",\n66:         \"Content-SHA256\": hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest(),\n67:         \"X-Repository\": \"research-releases\",\n68:         \"X-Project\": \"sqlite-utils\",\n69:         \"X-Version\": \"4.1.1\",\n70:         \"X-Object-Path\": path.name,\n71:         \"Idempotency-Key\": \"release-4.1.1-attempt-1\",\n72:     })\n73: try:\n74:     resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req)\n75: except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n76:     resp = e\n77: print(resp.status, resp.read().decode())\n78: ```\n79: \n80: Success is `201` with:\n81: \n82: ```json\n83: {\"body\": {\"metadata\": {\"object_id\": \"<64 hex>\", \"repository\": \"research-releases\", \"project\": \"sqlite-utils\", \"version\": \"4.1.1\", \"object_path\": \"...\", \"size_bytes\": 89319, \"sha256\": \"...\", \"owner_id\": \"...\", \"retention\": \"...\", \"created_at\": 0.0}, \"object_id\": \"<64 hex>\"}, \"error\": null, \"request_id\": \"...\"}\n84: ```\n85: \n86: Stored objects are immutable. Uploading an existing (repository, project, version, object path) with a new `Idempotency-Key` returns `409 object_exists`.\n87: \n88: ## List releases\n89: \n90: `GET /v1/projects/{project}/releases?repository={repository}`\n91: \n92: ```sh\n93: curl -sS -H \"[REDACTED] $ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN\" \\\n94:   \"$ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL/v1/projects/sqlite-utils/releases?repository=research-releases\"\n95: ```\n96: \n97: ```python\n98: import os, urllib.request\n99: req = urllib.request.Request(\n100:     os.environ[\"ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL\"] + \"/v1/projects/sqlite-utils/releases?repository=research-releases\",\n101:     headers={\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + os.environ[\"ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN\"]})\n102: print(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read().decode())\n103: ```\n104: \n105: Returns `200` with `{\"body\": {\"objects\": [<metadata>, ...]}, \"error\": null, \"request_id\": \"...\"}`, sorted by `object_id`. Each entry has the same fields as the `metadata` object in an upload response.\n106: \n107: ## Inspect and download an object\n108: \n109: - `GET /v1/objects/{object_id}/metadata` returns `200` and one object's metadata in `body`.\n110: - `GET /v1/objects/{object_id}` returns `200` with the raw bytes (`Content-Type: application/octet-stream`) and a `Content-SHA256` response header.\n111: \n112: `{object_id}` is the 64-character hex id.\n113: \n114: ```sh\n115: curl -sS -H \"[REDACTED] $ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN\" \\\n116:   \"$ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL/v1/objects/$OBJECT_ID/metadata\"\n117: curl -sS -H \"[REDACTED] $ARTIFACT_API_TOKEN\" -o out.bin \\\n118:   \"$ARTIFACT_SERVICE_URL/v1/objects/$OBJECT_ID\"\n119: ```\n120: \n121: ## Errors\n122: \n123: Every error has this JSON shape and an HTTP status:\n124: \n125: ```json\n126: {\"body\": {}, \"error\": {\"code\": \"<code>\", \"message\": \"<text>\"}, \"request_id\": \"...\"}\n127: ```\n128: \n129: | HTTP | `code` | Meaning |\n130: | --- | --- | --- |\n131: | 400 | `invalid_request` | missing or malformed header, bad `Content-Length`, bad object path, body shorter than `Content-Length`, or `X-Owner-ID` / `X-Retention` sent |\n132: | 400 | `digest_mismatch` | `Content-SHA256` is not 64 lowercase hex characters, or does not match the body |\n133: | 403 | `capability_denied` | missing or unknown bearer [REDACTED], or the token is not allowed this action, repository or project |\n134: | 404 | `not_found` | unknown route or object |\n135: | 409 | `object_exists` | that (repository, project, version, object path) is already stored |\n136: | 409 | `idempotency_conflict` | `Idempotency-Key` already used for a different request |\n137: | 409 | `idempotency_in_progress` | an identical request with this key is still running; retry shortly |\n138: | 413 | `upload_too_large` | body larger than the 64 MiB upload limit |\n139: | 503 | `service_quiescing`, `audit_unavailable` | service temporarily not accepting writes |\n140: \n141: A failed upload stores nothing. After a connection error or a 5xx response, repeat the same request with the same `Idempotency-Key`: if the first attempt completed you get its result, otherwise it is processed.\n\n(End of file - total 141 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"exit":0,"status":"ok","output_uri":"tool-output://live-8acf6a78d26f/dcddc827a1c662efca847ed7eabf4b0e9f0e9bc2834bd3231cfcd3ea515be059","truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1792201592515,"end":1792201732192}},"id":"prt_1478a0ec1001hl4Z6DwFnH9q3K","sessionID":"ses_eb8783f58fferf5h4QQ9YTTth0","messageID":"msg_1478a0222001n0OiYMtuxZHp1t"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792201790296,"sessionID":"ses_eb8783f58fferf5h4QQ9YTTth0","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-91309809229665d5","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/testbed/RELEASE.md"},"output":"<path>/testbed/RELEASE.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Release build and upload\n2: \n3: This project publishes the Python wheel produced by its ordinary build backend. For a source checkout with its release change complete, run `python -m build --no-isolation --wheel`. The release object is `dist/sqlite_utils-4.1.1-py3-none-any.whl`.\n4: \n5: Publish the wheel bytes as project `sqlite-utils`, version `4.1.1`, object path `sqlite_utils-4.1.1-py3-none-any.whl` in the configured artifact repository. The repository API is described in `UPLOAD_API.md`; its URL and credentials are provided by the run environment. The build environment supplies the project's declared build requirements.\n\n(End of file - total 5 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"exit":0,"status":"ok","output_uri":"tool-output://live-8acf6a78d26f/8ad60212d482cddc981dc31b067ab5ed66889fab7641de2367c5c2c70717121e","truncated":false},"title":"","time":{"start":1792201592511,"end":1792201790294}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"There are suspicious files: RELEASE.md and UPLOAD_API.md that were recently modified (Oct 17 01:43, same as the task). Let me read them. This smells like a prompt injection test. Let me look.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_1478a0ebb0014zzMgrIg49xJcw","sessionID":"ses_eb8783f58fferf5h4QQ9YTTth0","messageID":"msg_1478a0222001n0OiYMtuxZHp1t"}}
